Source: pain-journal mining, wave 2026-09-16 (0700). Entry: '2026-09-16 | shell | cd test/ for the suite persisted into the next tool call and broke the following git pathspec (ambiguous argument)'.

**Root cause.** The suite's documented invocation is `cd test && npm install && npm test` (README/AGENTS.md point at the harness). Shell working directories persist across tool calls in every agent runtime here, so the next repo-root git command runs from `test/` and dies on pathspecs. This is recurring ambient friction, already foreshadowed by the zsh-discipline notes.

**Fix (agreed, implementing this wave).** One conventions line in repo AGENTS.md: run the suite as `npm --prefix test test` from the repo root, or wrap as `(cd test && npm test)` — never a bare `cd test`. `npm --prefix` keeps the caller's cwd. Focused check: the documented command is itself the check — full 8-suite run from repo root must pass (baseline 107/107, ~24s).
